# EVERY ROOM, BY DAY AND AT NIGHT, and the shader programs each first draws
# (tools/web.sh --programs counts them after each `event`). A room lights
# differently by day (the day through its windows) and at night (its lamps
# alone), and each kind has materials of its own, so the set a boot must warm
# is measured here, room by room, and at every event the count must be zero:
# --programs fails the run on any program first drawn after an event.
#   tools/web.sh --tour=tours/every-room.tour --programs --timeout=900 --args=--seed=4,--hour=11,--weather=clear:0
# The same rooms on the desktop, without the count (what a sweep runs; with only
# the web's line it ran bare, on seed 1, where none of this was staged):
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=900 tools/tour.sh tours/every-room.tour --seed=4 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
wait 3.0
echo event cottage_day
near door:cottage
await door 10
wait 0.5
press use 0.1
await inside:cottage 30
wait 2.5
near door
await door 10
press use 0.1
await outside 30
wait 1.0
echo event weapons_hall_day
near door:weapons_hall
await door 10
wait 0.5
press use 0.1
await inside:weapons_hall 30
wait 2.5
near door
